  "observations": [
    "The current README corrects the eager-Liftoff retention figures to 458786 through 549124 bytes. The immutable R1 README preserves the stale r3 figures; replay R1 at ff3789f2.",
    "Nineteen logical modules include two byte-identical binaries (twins_inner_2 and separate_inner_1), so the engine retains eighteen NativeModules. Distinct digests are not required; the duplicate benefits from the engine cache.",
    "The roughly 1.93 ms cold figure measures decode/validation under the default lazy tier. Audit 119 observed roughly 8 ms with eager compilation in a separate three-process probe; neither is a comparative performance claim.",
    "The three redefinitions change constants and retain equal encoded sizes. Different-body-shape revisions are not exercised."
  ],
  "scope": "Select one generated function per module; integrate exact reviewed synchronous trusted-owner code-set validation, compilation and publication. No merged fallback, lazy profile, whole-bootstrap workload or code-reclamation claim.",
  "verification": "Every executable source pin unchanged; current README correction explicitly excluded from historical source-pin equality. Integrated bundle and dependencies execute the retained mapping/refusal/rollback and three-Worker redefinition/snapshot oracles byte-identically. Compiler and all prior runtime files unchanged; native R6/R6a and measurements reused by exact code identity.",
